{"_id":"6a2ff9f22204ffbc59e5a823","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"j4UHICw-niFv1RRlC-vk1","description":"# Customizing Plots\n\nSeaborn plots are customized through function parameters (palette, hue, size, style) and by accessing the underlying Matplotlib axes after creation. `sns.set_theme()` and `sns.set_style()` change the global appearance. Seaborn's theming system makes it easy to produce clean, publication-ready charts with minimal code.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Controlling figure aesthetics","url":"https://seaborn.pydata.org/tutorial/aesthetics.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb21"},{"type":"article","title":"5 Ways to Transform Your Seaborn Data Visualisations","url":"https://towardsdatascience.com/5-ways-to-transform-your-seaborn-data-visualisations-1ed2cb484e38/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb22"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T13:11:14.684Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/j4UHICw-niFv1RRlC-vk1.md"}